> MicroVAX II? Does anyone have a copy of the media?

I also have a II and right now it's running 5.5-2H4.
It has the usual TK50 and a 350MB ESDI disk. I have chosen VMS 5,
because I wanted a small and fast system on this old beast.
7.3 might fit on a small disk, but I usually want more than just
the plain VMS installed and with some layered products disk space
is used up rather quickly.
To get it up and running, I first installed a proper VMS installation
on a spare disk of a VAXstation 3100. Then I booted my normal VMS
installation for that 3100 from another disk and netbooted the
MicroVAX II into the cluster. Then I could BACKUP/IMAGE the new
VMS from the 3100 to the II. The procedure works nicely and you
don't have to rely on old tape drives.

Dennis

