Yes.

As your fans stop, replace them ASAP. A working PSU with dead fan will
die within hours.

Cut wires in the middle, pass heat shrink tubes, solder new fan
(respecting polarity), put tape if you did not have isolating tubes, all
done.

DEC PSU should be screwn up with normal screws (I have seen very funny
PSU with not-ordinary screws).

Soldering wires directly at proper place on board is possible, but, I
usually prefer cuttinf existing wires because:
- it is easier
- it is faster (no need to unscrew the board from cage)
- avoid doing mistakes (if iron touches other points by mistake)
- less heat to spend: it is always faster to solder a wire to a wire,
than to a board that have existing strips and solder
- no need to mark/remember wire location: wires stay in place, so, you
dont need to memorise which color goes where.

All fans have + and -, usually red and black (can be also brown, yellow,
 grey). Some have a third wire for speed sensing (grey, orange, green
... or many other possible colors).

YES /some/ PSU have speed sensor on their fan !

