> I already have that media. I would have to get it onto a TK50, not sure if 
> the OS will fit onto a 70MB RD53 though. Will check unless someone knows the 
> answer straight away?

Another reason to get a more modern VAX with CD-ROM drive.  70 MB is WAY 
to small.  In older versions of VMS, you could get by with 120 MB or so 
IF you didn't install everything and IF you installed it on a larger 
disk first and then used VMSTAILOR to cut it down.  Not fun.  (I think 
there was a special version of the RZ23 drive which was a few MB larger 
than normal so that one could put VMS on it.)

I use RZ28 disks (2 GB) for VAX system disks.  Even with lots of stuff 
installed, they are only about half full.  (In other words, you could 
get away with a 1-GB RZ26 if you are careful, but I would really 
recommend RZ28's.)  Of course, this assumes you have SCSI.  Again, you 
need a somewhat more modern VAX.

> However, now I remember what the real question is. I hope to get a DEQNA or 
> DELQA card for it so I can connect it to the network (if I can find one at a 
> hobbyist price), but for a DEQNA I believe that I need a VMS version prior 
> to 5.5, anyone know where I might get the media for that?

